meta {
  name: Update Profile - set role (sign-up completion)
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

post {
  url: {{coreBaseUrl}}:8101/
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{idToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "role": "staff"
  }
}

docs {
  functions-core: UpdateProfile (port 8101). role can only be set once, from
  "" to nursery|staff — this is the one-time sign-up-completion step
  (ARCHITECTURE.md v2 §1a "profiles.go"). Run this against the new user from
  auth/05-signup-new-user.bru AFTER manually creating its profiles/{uid} doc
  (see that request's docs) — running it against an already-seeded user
  (whose role is already set) will correctly fail with 409 ROLE_ALREADY_SET.
}
